ing amount. Working farm buildings may need a farm policy instead. Check your policy to see which structures are listed and how they are valued."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"My metal pole barn has hail dents. Will the insurer pay?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the policy. Some exclude cosmetic damage to metal roofing and siding, while others pay for dents that affect appearance. If the hail caused punctures or damaged seams and fasteners, that is usually treated as functional damage."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does flat Allen County farmland really change wind risk?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Open terrain allows wind to arrive with little to slow it, so homes and outbuildings can take the full force of thunderstorm gusts. That is one reason wind and hail claims are common in Northwest Ohio."}}],"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/lima-ohio/#faq"},{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance appraisal in Lima, Ohio","serviceType":"Insurance appraisal","description":"Lima, Ohio insurance appraiser for wind, hail and tornado claims in Allen County, from older city homes to farmsteads with barns and outbuildings.","provider":{"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Lima","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Ohio"}},"url":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/lima-ohio/","@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/lima-ohio/#service"}]}</script>
